  "circulation": "Main yard/mess/bunkhouse loop is short and sheltered on one side. Sawmill/shed loop is more exposed. Two cabin-trail returns avoid a long compulsory dead end. Inspection deck is optional; all rites stay on the ground.",
  "systems": "Mill, domestic and service electrical districts; timber stacks break sightlines without moving between graphics presets. Wind, loose roofing and inert machinery produce ordinary sounds; any powered event needs a real source/state.",
  "campaign": "Payroll omissions in stores, manifest in sawmill office and personal accounts in bunkhouse. Proposed shipping connection to Dead Man's Claim is a found-document thread, never automatic ghost evidence.",
  "refine": [
    "First remote construction exemplar after the established house reference: prove all tools, three rites and human/AI ghost access here.",
    "Subdivide sawmill into believable machine and circulation bays while retaining the diagram footprint.",
    "Inspect primary logging-camp building references before shell work; proposed metres are not historical measurements."
  ],
